Thought: First, I need to get the magnesium structure from Materials Project using the provided ID (mp-153) and save it as a CIF file.
Action: get_structure_from_mp_text
Action Input: {"mp_id": "mp-153", "file_path": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/claude_35/react/melting/workflow/tasks/magnesium_melting_trial_1/Mg.cif"}

Thought: Now I need to convert the CIF file to a LAMMPS data file using the specified atom_style "atomic".
Action: convert_structure_to_lammps_data
Action Input: {"structure_path": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/claude_35/react/melting/workflow/tasks/magnesium_melting_trial_1/Mg.cif", "output_file": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/claude_35/react/melting/workflow/tasks/magnesium_melting_trial_1/Mg.data", "atom_style": "atomic"}

Thought: I need to check available EAM potentials for Magnesium to use in the simulation.
Action: list_files
Action Input: {"path": "/potentials", "recursive": false}

Thought: Let me check the EAM directory for Magnesium potentials.
Action: list_files
Action Input: {"path": "/potentials/EAM", "recursive": false}

Thought: I found the Mg_Zhou04.eam.alloy potential. Let me verify its metadata to ensure it's suitable for Magnesium.
Action: get_potential_metadata
Action Input: {"file_path": "/potentials/EAM/Mg_Zhou04.eam.alloy"}

Thought: Now I can run the LAMMPS simulation with the created input script.
Action: run_lammps
Action Input: {"input_file": "/results/2_AUGUST_2025/claude_35/react/melting/workflow/tasks/magnesium_melting_trial_1/melting.in"}

Thought: I need to read the log file to find the final density value.
Action: read_file
Action Input: {"path": "melting.log"}
